# The build context of rust/Dockerfile is the repo root (docker build -f
# rust/Dockerfile .): only what its stages read goes in, so an unrelated
# change doesn't invalidate the cache and the context stays small.
*

# The pnpm workspace, for the platform SPA and the sign portal.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!patches
!packages
!apps/web/platform
!apps/web/sign-portal

# The Rust workspace, for the backend.
!rust/rust-toolchain.toml
!rust/Cargo.toml
!rust/Cargo.lock
!rust/clippy.toml
!rust/.cargo
!rust/catalogs
!rust/crates
!rust/modules
!rust/bins
!rust/docker

# Never: installs, build output, local state, tests.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/target
**/.turbo
**/.wrangler
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars
rust/**/tests
# The Drizzle migrations (~290 MB of SQL and snapshots): no frontend reads them.
packages/core/db/drizzle
apps/web/platform/docs
apps/web/platform/e2e
apps/web/platform/playwright-report
apps/web/platform/test-results
